OL,3,GNEWSATwo teenagers in hospital with
OL,4,Ameningitis B
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo teenagers are receiving treatment
OL,7,Fin hospital after contracting
OL,8,Fmeningitis B.
OL,10,FThe UK Health Security Agency (UKHSA)
OL,11,Fconfirmed it was investigating two
OL,12,Fconfirmed cases in the Suffolk area"
OL,13,Fbut said "the risk to the wider public
OL,14,Fremains low".
OL,16,FIt said the teenagers were "currently
OL,17,Freceiving treatment in hospital where
OL,18,Fthey are recovering well".
